      "description": "DT-In / DT-Intro replaced by Theorem 4 (Def6): [P-K2-467] refers to the restricted rule 'DT-In' and [P-K2-464] formulates (DT-Intro) as an inference rule ('from φ ∧ D(φ) infer T(φ)'). Target instead assumes Def6 (∀ φ, 𝓢 ⊢ D φ 🡒 (T φ 🡘 φ)), which matches Theorem 4 in [P-K2-464] (and includes the unused T φ 🡒 φ direction); using the internal conditional is necessary here because σ is only an assumption in step (2), not an unconditionally proved sentence."
    },
    {
      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Propositional abstraction and omission of K → T (K1): Whereas the source passages work in the specific arithmetical theory DTK with quantifiers, Gödel coding, and K1 (K → T), Target quantifies abstractly over any classical propositional system 𝓢 with arbitrary functions T, K, D and sentence parameters. In particular, K → T (which [P-K2-467] notes is present in DTK and used in step (1)) is not assumed as a principle (Def4), and step (1) along with the reflection, incompleteness, deduction, and extensionality steps are supplied as six unanalyzed propositional hypotheses."
    },
