      "severity": "minor",
      "description": "Provable determinateness vs. determinateness: Target requires meta-level provability of determinateness in 𝓢 (𝓢 ⊢ D σ and 𝓢 ⊢ D (σ 🡒 G)) to derive 𝓢 ⊢ ∼σ, matching how DK-Intro operates as a proof rule in DTK, whereas [P-K2-467] speaks informally of the statements being 'determinate'."
