  "summary": "Target diverges from [P-K2-467] in two major ways: it formalizes sufficiency ('if determinate, then ∼σ is provable') rather than the source's necessity claim ('legitimate only if determinate'), and it assumes determinateness for σ and σ 🡒 G rather than the two sentences explicitly named in [P-K2-467] (σ 🡒 S' and K (σ 🡒 G)) without any axioms linking them. It also makes several minor idealizations, including using Theorem 4 (Def6) in place of the rule DT-Intro and absorbing K → T and the arithmetical steps into abstract propositional bridging hypotheses."
